# For configuration of EC2 and EFS 

Link : https://digitalcloud.training/mounting-efs-on-ec2-instance/

# Note: Follow  above link for creation of security group and EFS. 

Then follow below notes. 

# For ubuntu  :

https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-set-up-an-nfs-mount-on-ubuntu-18-04

sudo apt update
sudo apt install nfs-kernel-server
sudo apt-get install nfs-common

# create directory to mount: 

mkdir  /efs

# Using NFS to mount  : 

for eg: 

sudo mount -t nfs4 -o nfsvers=4.1,rsize=1048576,wsize=1048576,hard,timeo=600,retrans=2,noresvport fs-00aefc9a8069dbe77.efs.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com:/ efs

# For linux 

sudo yum -y update  
sudo reboot
sudo yum -y install nfs-utils 

mkdir  /efs

# Using NFS to mount  : 

for eg: 

sudo mount -t nfs4 -o nfsvers=4.1,rsize=1048576,wsize=1048576,hard,timeo=600,retrans=2,noresvport fs-00aefc9a8069dbe77.efs.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com:/ efs

# To make EFS mount presistent :

Link: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/52558062/auto-mounting-efs-on-ec2-instance 

# Make entry in fstab of EFS:
path : /etc/fstab 

for eg: fs-1234567c.efs.us-west-1.amazonaws.com:/ /mnt/heider nfs4 defaults,_netdev 0 0

# Note: fs-XXXXXXX is EFS DNS . 

